  "body": "### Summary\n\nThe composer hosted tests wait until their frames settle (#1114), but if the frames never settle the tests go on and measure a frame in mid-move, which can still meet the 0.5 pt tolerances. Make an unsettled layout fail loudly. (Opus review round 3 on #1114, Low 1 + detail; not seen as a flake yet.)\n\n### Scope\n\n- `App/SwiftHFRTests/Composer/ComposerLayoutHostedTests.swift:60-67`: after the polling loop, `try #require(steady >= 4, \"frames never settled: \\(box.frames)\")`.\n- Optionally also require `box.layout` unchanged between reads (test 1 asserts on `layout.text`, `editorHeight`, `textCardHeight`).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A mutation that keeps the frames moving (e.g. an animation that never ends) makes the suite red with the \"never settled\" message; the suite is green on iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone Duo.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
